      "text": "To solve the given problem, we need to compute \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the solutions of the equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x = 9\\). We can use the relationships between the roots and coefficients of the polynomial to simplify the computation.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the polynomial equation:\n\\[x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0.\\]\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\), we know:\n- The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = 5\\),\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\),\n- The product of the roots \\(rst = 9\\).\n\nWe need to compute \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). We can rewrite this expression using the fact that \\(s\\), \\(r\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial. Specifically, we need to find:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}.\n\\]\n\nBy combining the fractions, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot ts + tr \\cdot tr}{rst} = \\frac{r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2}{rst}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity for the sum of squares:\n\\[r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t).\\]\n\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[rs + rt + st = 6,\\]\n\\[rst = 9,\\]\n\\[r + s + t = 5.\\]\n\nWe get:\n\\[r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54.\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2}{rst} = \\frac{-54}{9} = -6.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}.\n\\]",
