      "text": "To solve the problem, we start with the given polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\) and its roots \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships between the roots and the coefficients of the polynomial:\n\n1. \\(r + s + t = 5\\)\n2. \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\)\n3. \\(rst = 9\\)\n\nWe need to compute the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). To do this, we can rewrite the expression in terms of \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs \\cdot rs}{rst \\cdot rst} = \\frac{(rs)^3}{(rst)^2}\n\\]\n\nUsing Vieta's formula \\(rst = 9\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(rs)^3}{(rst)^2} = \\frac{(rs)^3}{9^2} = \\frac{(rs)^3}{81}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\(rs\\). We can use the identity for the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time, which is \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\). We can express \\(rs\\) in terms of \\(r\\) and \\(s\\) as follows:\n\n\\[\n(rs)^2 + (rt)^2 + (ts)^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2(rt^2 + rt^2 + tst + tr^2 + tr^2) + 4rst^2 = 6^2 - 2(r^2s^2 + r^2s^2 + r^2s^2) + 4 \\cdot 9 = 36 - 2 \\cdot 3(r^2s^2) + 36 = 72 - 6(r^2s^2)\n\\]\n\nHowever, a simpler approach is to directly use the expression for \\((rs)^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(rs)^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2(r^2s^2 + r^2s^2 + r^2s^2) + 4rst^2 = 6^2 - 2(r^2s^2 + r^2s^2 + r^2s^2) + 4 \\cdot 9 = 36 - 2(r^2s^2) + 36 = 72 - 2(r^2s^2)\n\\]\n\nBut instead, we can use the fact that \\(rs = \\sqrt{(rs)^2}\\) and \\(rt = \\sqrt{(rt)^2}\\) and \\(ts = \\sqrt{(ts)^2}\\). We need to find \\((rs)^3\\):\n\n\\[\n(rs)^3 = (rs)^2 \\cdot rs = (rs)^2 \\cdot rs = (rs)^2 \\cdot rs = (rs)^2 \\cdot rs = (rs)^2 \\cdot rs\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\) and \\(rst = 9\\), so we can substitute these values into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{(rs)^3}{81} = \\frac{(rs)^3}{81} = \\frac{6}{9} = \\frac{2}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\n\\[\n\\bo